<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Electricity Sphere</h1>
<p>The spells of the electricity sphere call down and hurl lightning. How strongly one strikes depends on your magic and your skill in that spell.
</p><p>The sphere itself is a category. It can't be practised: it rises by itself to half your best spell in it. It counts when you resist: against an electricity spell aimed at you, you defend with your brain and the better of your electricity sphere or half your skill in that spell (see <a cmd='#'>Help Spheres</a>). Lightning finds its way past a shield: no shield is of any use against these spells. To resist electricity better, see <a cmd='#'>Help Electricity Resistance</a>; dragons may also breathe lightning (see <a cmd='#'>Help Breath</a>).
</p><p>The spells, and who teaches them (guild level):
</p>
<pre>call lightning     no guild teaches it
lightning breath   no guild teaches it
electrical shock   sorcerer 3
jolt               sorcerer 16
lightning bolt     sorcerer 30
lightning storm    sorcerer 160
</pre>
<p>Each spell has its own help: help and the spell's name.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Spheres</a>
